                  "marginLeft": "auto"
                }
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "s2t1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>As the Commercial Vehicle Safety Alliance’s Brake Safety Week is scheduled for Aug. 23-29, inspectors are putting a special focus on drums and rotors during this year’s event. Brake drum and rotor issues may affect a vehicle’s brake efficiency. Broken pieces of drums and rotors may become dislodged from the vehicle during travel and damage other vehicles or result in injuries or fatalities to the motoring public.</strong>",
                    "width": "full"
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "paddingTop": 0,
                      "paddingBottom": 0,
                      "marginBottom": "22"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s2h2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "HERE’S TIPS TO HELP ESNURE YOUR DRUMS AND ROTORS ARE READY TO PASS INSPECTION:",
                    "headingLevel": 3
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "paddingTop": 0,
                      "paddingBottom": 0,
                      "marginBottom": "22"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s2h3",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "drum inspection tips",
                    "headingLevel": 3
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "paddingTop": 0,
                      "paddingBottom": 0,
                      "marginBottom": "22"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s2r4",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0,
                    "stackOn": "never"
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginTop": "0",
                      "marginRight": "0",
                      "marginBottom": "22",
                      "marginLeft": "0",
                      "paddingLeft": "22",
                      "display": "grid",
                      "rowGap": "14",
                      "columnGap": "14"
                    }
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "s2c5",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "s2t6",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Check for cracks. Small hairline cracks caused by normal heating and cooling is common, but structural cracks typically require replacement.",
                            "width": "full"
                          },
                          "styles": {
                            "base": {
                              "paddingTop": 0,
                              "paddingBottom": 0
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "s2c7",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "s2t8",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Measure drum diameter. Drums worn beyond their maximum allowable diameter need to be replaced, as excessive diameter reduces effectiveness and contribute to out-of-service violations.",
                            "width": "full"
                          },
                          "styles": {
                            "base": {
                              "paddingTop": 0,
                              "paddingBottom": 0
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "s2c9",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "s2t10",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Look for heat damage. Be vigilant of blue/dark discoloration, hot spots, heat checking focused in one area, scoring or gouging.",
                            "width": "full"
                          },
                          "styles": {
                            "base": {
                              "paddingTop": 0,
                              "paddingBottom": 0
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "s2c11",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "s2t12",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Check for contamination. Inspect drums for oil, grease, and wheel-seal leakage. Contamination can significantly reduce brake performance.",
                            "width": "full"
                          },
                          "styles": {
                            "base": {
                              "paddingTop": 0,
                              "paddingBottom": 0
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "s2i13",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "image": {
                      "src": "https://www.truckcountry.com/efs/wp/domains/www.truckcountry.com/wp-content/uploads/elementor/thumbs/Aftermarket_P4_Wheel-hubs-and-brakes-9-scaled-e1755546670566-ragcquvzjq6sklah2dm54b50o173xtp4zs17gpi55s.jpg",
                      "alt": "Vehicle Brake"
                    },
                    "width": "full"
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "paddingTop": 0,
                      "paddingBottom": 0,
                      "marginBottom": "22"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s2h14",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Rotor Inspection Tips",
                    "headingLevel": 3
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "paddingTop": 0,
                      "paddingBottom": 0,
                      "marginBottom": "22"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s2r15",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0,
                    "stackOn": "never"
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginTop": "0",
                      "marginRight": "0",
                      "marginBottom": "0",
                      "marginLeft": "0",
                      "paddingLeft": "22",
                      "display": "grid",
                      "rowGap": "14",
                      "columnGap": "14"
                    }
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "s2c16",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "s2t17",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Check rotor thickness. Measure rotor thickness at multiple locations, as uneven thickness can cause vibration and poor braking performance.",
                            "width": "full"
                          },
                          "styles": {
                            "base": {
                              "paddingTop": 0,
                              "paddingBottom": 0
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "s2c18",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "s2t19",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Inspect for surface cracks. Be on the lookout for heat and structural cracks, as well as cracks extending to cooling vanes or edges.",
                            "width": "full"
                          },
                          "styles": {
                            "base": {
                              "paddingTop": 0,
                              "paddingBottom": 0
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "s2c20",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "s2t21",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Look for excessive scoring or grooving. Deep grooves may indicate metal-to-metal contact, work pads, or foreign material trapped in the brake assembly.",
                            "width": "full"
                          },
                          "styles": {
                            "base": {
                              "paddingTop": 0,
                              "paddingBottom": 0
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "s2c22",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "s2t23",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Check for heat damage. Bluing, heat spots or warping can lead to reduced braking efficiency.",
                            "width": "full"
                          },
                          "styles": {
                            "base": {
                              "paddingTop": 0,
                              "paddingBottom": 0
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "s2c24",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "s2t25",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Verify the rotor mounting condition. Look for loose mounting hardware, corrosion and rotor runout concerns, as improper mounting can lead to uneven wear and brake pulsation.",
                            "width": "full"
                          },
                          "styles": {
                            "base": {
                              "paddingTop": 0,
                              "paddingBottom": 0
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
